  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_7e2bc0f7953b4a29a2f7b57b732f8347",
      "statement": "No measurement is written down in the evaluation modules: every expected number is read from a checked-in expectation file, so no line in eval code can be edited to turn a red row green — the only literals are the spec's gate thresholds, pinned in code so relaxing one is a reviewable release rather than an environment edit.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/vsir/eval/acceptance.py#L10-L24",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:827ea64c9f90f4eb7d48793d8b72ac15c17071a5abffb0a736b4ceb902a09a92:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/vsir/eval/corpus.py#L13-L21",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c2db438c848c1323359ac11ae27265ede35faa682671ae70f1f5d402264ec25f:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_a01279be9f8a4f7593a5921ec81e15c4",
      "statement": "The hand-written synthetic corpus stores only each page's text and the model's claims and derives the page record from them, because a hand-authored record could contradict itself; its points are upserted with an empty vector map so the corpus exercises the exact surface and nothing that ranks.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/vsir/eval/synthetic.py#L10-L23",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:26244789f1d8bd7d8c1d945f66c3c4c521b2a9408f9edc182d4eeb32631e4363:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_3a0b643f6ee24d51831db39270ade070",
      "statement": "The generated 42-page corpus wires six specific hazards into the page geometry — folds across sections, a printed-label offset, a code below the footer that a cropped raster would miss, a scanned cover over a born-digital body, a code read off the facing sheet, and a code printed on no page — so the pipeline's failure modes are exercised rather than described.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/vsir/eval/synthetic_pdf.py#L1-L31",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f149d45bbfb6a895aa6e049bb705f827c087b33dfcbee966b8dc74471bfb1bf2:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_4f69e367dee843e594af4ff2f663df63",
      "statement": "The generated 150-page corpus differs from the 42-page one in exactly one load-bearing way: it declares no contents page, so the window planner has no chapter boundary and falls to the fold-at-the-cap rung, producing five windows of thirty — the only place that rung is exercised end to end.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/vsir/eval/synthetic_large.py#L1-L30",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:dbb797015fb148e0db2ca81e51ce55f7a35cd30d7f629b90448922f5881c24df:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_541c75edcced4b06a7e76dc6fb9db49e",
      "statement": "Frozen extraction fixtures are keyed so they move when the model id, the prompt version, the dpi or the extraction schema moves, which is deliberate: a schema edit means the model was asked a different question and its old answer does not contain the new field.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/vsir/eval/synthetic_pdf.py#L32-L45",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:32b31583407b9d9c3b1892fbab7326170a25d261840559718970a062c45b8321:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_4038ae273d7049a89c7eb657ff4dea94",
      "statement": "The ported legacy fixture is read-only and carries a ledger of every file with its sha256, so the fixture's integrity can be proved even where the original source tree is not mounted.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/vsir/eval/legacy.py#L11-L23",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:560655460e576d21062951c7c918f4b222315620261c35d414a51efd23698f34:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_544e5adf37ce4176af1c1a8530a82f99",
      "statement": "One export run of the previous implementation is pinned with its reason recorded: the other candidate runs withheld labels that a later fix backs, so their negative sets are polluted by a defect already corrected.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/vsir/eval/legacy.py#L24-L32",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:516f185bb9070f64e54ed4ac90f140264f1858c696fc68593c2a6963a02fdfdd:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_e55fff4a7b8c42fc8ba448ef00ce1dd8",
      "statement": "The legacy baseline exposes an observable projection of the text layer rather than the text layer itself — for each page, the identifier strings the old gate found in that page's own text — and nothing the model said is included in it.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/vsir/eval/legacy.py#L34-L45",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:fc080cf38ab72e3e099336207e593257a704387bc2625b97f677e550c61d701f:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_9d9fc1c28e69498698b016c0156a75a1",
      "statement": "vsir eval acceptance runs three sections — synthetic, parity and real — where parity's gains are printed and never failed, and the real section's unmeasurable rows skip by name with the skip count printed in the summary.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/vsir/eval/acceptance.py#L26-L44",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6aba85b17c581c6169b7c52f043d1efc77309c9dfe81cca1503d6372dc3476d1:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_31bd12fbb30344809611f3ea1fa2461c",
      "statement": "The acceptance command writes down the spec's own text — the label list and its order, the page and window counts, the weak-absence constant — and asserts it against the checked-in expectation table, because a table that had drifted from the spec would make every measurement below it meaningless.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/vsir/eval/acceptance.py#L17-L24",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:12cb8cfe8cdce1f9d36224712e8dc6450cba15e5ddd4f9c40992cec9f1bd57de:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_bbdc127b567443af9691964e352010a4",
      "statement": "Every acceptance section seeds a collection of its own, queries it and drops it, so the serving collection is never touched and no path can reach a model.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/vsir/eval/acceptance.py#L45-L48",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1341d99ee141c7275bede039d9adbebfb30a830ef5195deb107a259e7f8400e6:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_07c5dd276b334ae58c173920ca0da8c9",
      "statement": "The abstention eval puts one hundred one-character-off codes through the exact surface and the confirming check, and can be pointed at a live indexed corpus in a read-only mode that performs no upsert, delete or collection creation.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/vsir/eval/abstention.py#L1-L27",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a5f01bf847712285f94b3be6be9acd4b5376a63d2b0be276f64bbe20cb59d87d:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_ba4e6063b38b44df87396f2e3bc60f8f",
      "statement": "The abstention eval includes a control row looking up the real codes the fakes were mutated from, because a corpus that answered nothing at all would otherwise pass every absence assertion — making a broken index indistinguishable from a correctly abstaining one.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/vsir/eval/abstention.py#L29-L35",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:68dd5df1e509d3b61bb340bd44402ae831fe222b8f2772e5618df27624c97018:"
