    },
    {
      "id": "claim_7f7d2fea11734b4a9cdc04f9b7d51f83",
      "statement": "The corpus evaluation pins five gates transcribed from the specification — code_precision at 1.00 as a P0 stop, code_recall at 0.95 and blocked below 0.90, abstention_correctness at 1.00 as a P0 stop, alarm_label_hit at 0.99 and xref_resolve at 0.99.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/vsir/eval/corpus.py#L151-L160",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:49fbfce914086d6644909dca16271871cb2c8888da4ee6f3933c226f67876fd9:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_0c27e45cc6dc43af9c0bd733492ecc6c",
      "statement": "The abstention_correctness floor is pinned in two modules and the two are asserted equal at import time, so one gate cannot drift into two numbers.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/vsir/eval/corpus.py#L162-L170",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ee029828ce81c4346f448fd8fb43c5911d7c7d259b4c0490540664c6fc968756:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_3385386845864a8fb78256c108d42bdc",
      "statement": "Both code ratios are counted over (code, page) pairs rather than per code, because a code found on the right page and also on a wrong one would score as found under a per-code reading — and the injury the system exists to prevent is the wrong page.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/vsir/eval/corpus.py#L23-L30",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:58401fc56ddf76e33f9218673695ebb871b61c73eea9cfbf878bbe6c49d2aa02:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_33393682e75545b0addb609c14be6679",
      "statement": "Each metric row prints its denominator and the smallest non-zero shortfall the set can register, and a target metric whose resolution is coarser than its gate's tolerance is marked underpowered; a safety metric at a 1.00 floor is never marked underpowered because \"no miss in n\" is exactly what that gate asks.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/vsir/eval/corpus.py#L32-L36",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0b4e2c5888dce04fdb455dcd8aee4ac7e3ec4459053e954bc3ad5655061647eb:"
